## T3 — Fail-closed create and fence budgets with winning-insert quota
Reasoning: D1 makes replays quota-free, which needs separate, non-bypassable budgets; the current limiter is fail-open 
and counts attempts, not insertions.
Task: The insertion quota is charged in the same transaction as a winning insertion (once among concurrent same-key 
requests; never more stored messages than the quota with distinct keys at the boundary; not charged for replays); 
every authenticated create request — including malformed bodies, early-validation failures, replays, and quota losers 
— consumes a per-user request budget whose charge survives an insertion rollback; fence/lookup calls consume their own 
per-user budget (replacing the T2 fail-open 'message:fence' limiter, including the fence step inside a 
generation-carrying create); any exhausted budget returns 429; a budget that cannot be checked refuses the request as 
429 (D4 planning decision).
Done when: The AC-009 route-level clauses hold on the local database, including under a real limiter 
permission/availability failure.
