-- Phase 5 T3 / FR-008, AC-009, AC-035
-- (spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience): the message INSERTION QUOTA
-- is charged by the winning insertion, in the insertion's own transaction.
--
-- Budgets (POST /api/messages/create and /api/messages/fence, see
-- src/lib/auth/rate-limit.ts for the numbers). All three use the existing
-- fixed-window counter public.check_rate_limit (20260612190000):
--   * 'message:create-request' (request budget): charged by the create route
--     for EVERY authenticated request — malformed bodies, validation failures,
--     replays and quota losers included — through its own check_rate_limit
--     call, i.e. its own committed transaction BEFORE any insertion, so a
--     rolled-back insertion never refunds it.
--   * 'message:fence' (fence budget): charged by the fence route for every
--     authenticated call and by the fence step of a generation-carrying create.
--   * 'message:create' (insertion quota): charged HERE, inside
--     public.create_message_attempt, only after its INSERT won and passed the
--     commit-time fence check, immediately before the function returns (and
--     PostgREST commits). Consequences:
--       - a replay (created=false), a lost same-key race (the loser's INSERT
--         waits for the winner and then replays) and any refusal (fenced,
--         MESSAGE_DELETED, validation) never charge it;
--       - a refused charge (quota exhausted) raises RATE_LIMITED and rolls the
--         whole insertion back (no message, no attachment link, uploads stay
--         pending, attempt state unchanged), and its own counter increment is
--         rolled back with it;
--       - concurrent insertions of distinct keys serialize on the counter row
--         (INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE row lock, held to commit), so at a
--         quota boundary no more messages commit than the quota allows;
--       - a charge that cannot be made (function missing or revoked, counter
--         table error, lock timeout, deadlock) raises RATE_LIMIT_UNAVAILABLE
--         and rolls the insertion back: the route answers 429 (fail-closed,
--         D4 planning decision). A statement_timeout (query_canceled, which
--         an EXCEPTION WHEN OTHERS block cannot catch) still rolls the whole
--         insertion back; the route answers 500 and nothing is stored.
--     The limit and window come from the caller (p_insert_quota_limit,
--     p_insert_quota_window_seconds; both NULL = no charge). The action name is
--     fixed to 'message:create' so a Phase 4 server deployed during the
--     rollout, which charges the same counter at its route for every create,
--     shares one quota with this build.
--
