 168: ## 10. Constraints and assumptions
 169: 
 170: ### Constraints
 171: - Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict, Supabase, TanStack Query; reuse existing hooks, repositories, routes, 
and query keys rather than parallel implementations.
 172: - Identity: RLS compares `users.supabase_uid` with `auth.uid()::text`; foreign keys use `users.id`; messages 
link to rooms through `conversations.room_id`.
 173: - Browsers: Chrome and Edge desktop (automated E2E); Firefox desktop (verified). Safari and mobile not required.
 174: - No service worker; background notifications are page-level only.
 175: - No message text, names, or identifiers in metrics (BR-013); no external analytics service.
 176: - The sign-out confirmation must not change the Presence logout sequence (presence-safety rules apply to that 
touch point).
 177: - Online database changes only at phase end with explicit authorization (BR-014); the hosted app currently runs 
the pre-Phase-4 build until the owner deploys, so new server contracts must stay compatible with that build and with 
the Phase 4 build until deployment: unkeyed legacy message writes and existing RPC/route signatures keep working 
against the migrated database.
 178: - Repository test policy (BR-015); type-check, lint, and build must pass.
 179: - Timing parameters chosen under the owner's delegation (D4) and adjustable in planning only with owner 
approval: claim request timeout 30 s, lease 45 s, metrics batch ≤ 50 events / 16 KB, one metrics delivery in flight, 5 
s metrics abort.
 180: 
 181: ### Assumptions
 182: - None beyond the user-confirmed answers and owner decisions recorded in `state.md`.
 183: 
 184: ## 11. Edge cases and failure modes
 185: 
 186: | Case | Expected behavior |
 187: |---|---|
 188: | Tab closed right after pressing send, before server confirmation | Item is already in the outbox; on next load 
it is fenced and delivered once (AC-040). |
 189: | Request stored but response lost | Item becomes unknown; fence finds it stored; resolves as delivered; never 
offered for cancel or expired (AC-038, AC-042). |
 190: | Original create blocked before its INSERT, or still in the network, while another tab fences | The fence wins; 
the older generation can no longer commit; the item is resent once or cancelled/expired without a late duplicate 
(AC-045). |
 191: | Stale fence arrives after a takeover | Rejected as an older generation; the newer attempt is unaffected 
(AC-045). |
 192: | Hung holder when connectivity returns | Its attempt is superseded at once; D1 deadline holds (AC-041). |
 193: | Two tabs come online together | One drain claim per conversation; only the oldest unresolved item is eligible; 
no overlapping create requests for that conversation; each stored and shown once, in order (AC-005). |
 194: | Owning tab closes or hangs mid-request | Closed or lease expired: another tab fences and finishes once; while 
the lease is live no other tab dispatches (AC-041). |
 195: | Cancel races a claim | Exactly one wins; a cancelled item is never dispatched; a dispatched item cannot be 
cancelled (AC-006). |
 196: | Lost access before reconnect | First item fails definitively with text; later items of that conversation wait; 
other conversations deliver (AC-007). |
 197: | Access regained after failure | "Tentar de novo" delivers it, then the waiting items in order (AC-008). |
 198: | Other definitive outcomes (404, 400, 413, 422) and 5xx | Definitive → failed with text; 5xx → unknown → fence 
(AC-046). |
 199: | `CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED` | Failed; "Tentar de novo" resends the content under a new key, once (AC-043). |
 200: | Server rate limit during drain; concurrent same-key requests | Items stay pending, retried automatically; 
quota charged once per stored message; replays/fences use a separate budget (AC-009). |
 201: | Laptop asleep > 24 h | Not-stored items become "expirada"; stored ones resolve as delivered (AC-010, AC-042). |
 202: | Offline attachment / voice | Upload failure: per-file error + retry; create failure after upload: Phase 4 
composer failure; nothing in the outbox (AC-011). |
 203: | IndexedDB unavailable or write fails | Nothing dispatched; text stays in the composer with the storage message 
(D5) (AC-039). |
 204: | Identical texts sent twice; Realtime arrives before the HTTP response | One bubble per message, matched by key 
(AC-050). |
 205: | Account switched while a drain is paused or a response is in flight | Drain stops; no dispatch as the new 
user; late responses discarded; server rejects any request whose sender differs (AC-044, AC-047). |
 206: | Session ends without Sair; other user signs in | Other user never sees/sends A's items; A's items drain after 
A signs in (AC-012). |
 207: | Temporary Auth failure (401 with valid client session) | Treated as transient; retried; not held or deleted 
(AC-012). |
 208: | Sair with unsent items | Dialog; Cancelar has no side effects at any entry point; Sair mesmo stops drains 
everywhere and deletes the outbox; late responses do not resurrect items (AC-013, AC-047). |
 209: | Realtime drop < 5 s | No "Reconectando…" banner (AC-014). |
 210: | Only the conversation-list stream fails | Banner after 5 s and polling after 30 s follow its health; recovered 
independently (AC-015, AC-016). |
 211: | Stale poll returns after a newer Realtime update | Newer/enriched state kept; no duplicates (AC-048). |
 212: | Realtime down > 30 s, tab hidden | No polling; on visible, fetch immediately then every 15 s (AC-016). |
 213: | Typist closes the tab or leaves the conversation mid-typing | Indicator disappears ≤ 5 s (AC-017). |
 214: | Anon, outsider, public-topic, or removed-member typing access | Refused / no events; removed member's app 
leaves at once; tampered client bounded by D3 (AC-019). |
 215: | Forged mention IDs, plain "@name", changed mentions on replay, recipient removed before replay | No mention 
for non-members/self/plain text; changed composition → 409; unchanged replay returns the stored message (AC-024, 
AC-046). |
 216: | Recipient removed or account switched after commit but before the notification is shown | No notification once 
the app has the removal/switch signal; a removal not yet received at the final check is the accepted D6 race (AC-049). 
|
 217: | Manual retry of an expired item hits 429 or an unknown outcome | New 24 h window: retried/fenced automatically 
(AC-010). |
 218: | Partial reads by others during a Realtime-only outage | Receipt summaries and open reader details update via 
polling (AC-016). |
 219: | Hidden tab receives a mention event first while another tab views that conversation | No notification 
(AC-026). |
 220: | Malicious, oversized, hanging, or sustained metrics traffic | Rejected or dropped; route rate-limited; 
messaging unaffected (AC-028, AC-029). |
 221: | Restored conversation no longer accessible | Conversation list opens without error (AC-032). |
 222: 
 223: ## 12. Security, privacy, compliance, and abuse considerations
 224: - Outbox content lives only in the user's browser, scoped to the application user ID, fenced against account 
switches on the client and on the server (expected-sender check on create and fence), and deleted on confirmed 
explicit sign-out.
 225: - The fence/lookup call acts only on the caller's own message for that key, never creates a message, and is 
rejected for anon users and for other users' keys.
 226: - Every create request consumes a per-user request budget and fence/lookup calls their own, so the 
insertion-quota exemption for replays (D1) cannot be used for unlimited traffic.
 227: - Typing topics are private and members-only for join and send (Realtime RLS with `users.supabase_uid = 
auth.uid()::text` → `users.id`); the app leaves within 5 s of a removal; residual receive/send exposure of tampered 
removed-member clients accepted (D3, D6).
 228: - Mentions are validated and stored server-side in the message transaction; clients cannot write them directly; 
only members can read them; notifications are re-authorized right before emission (residual race accepted, D6).
 229: - Notifications never leak content of conversations the user is not (or no longer) a member of.
 230: - Metrics: closed enums, bounded numbers and sizes, server-derived version, per-user rate limit, no free text 
(BR-013); unauthenticated requests are rejected and produce no metric log line.
 231: - `mark_conversation_read` membership check and `anon` revoke on `get_unread_counts` close two Phase 4 findings.
 232: - No service-role key in client code; service-role use never replaces application authorization checks.
 233: - Every migration, RLS/Realtime policy, repository, and API route change passes the Supabase/RLS review gate.
